1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,000


2
00:01:01,560 --> 00:01:06,280
Taming The Husband

3
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:08,920
Episode 8

4
00:01:10,920 --> 00:01:12,800
What are you doing? Get out!

5
00:01:13,080 --> 00:01:14,880
Where are your manners?
I'm your sister-in-law!

6
00:01:14,960 --> 00:01:17,200
You wish!
You're vile, shameless, and disgusting!

7
00:01:17,280 --> 00:01:18,440
You call yourself my sister-in-law?

8
00:01:18,520 --> 00:01:20,040
-Someone--
-Shut up!

9
00:01:21,520 --> 00:01:22,600
Baozhu,

10
00:01:23,120 --> 00:01:24,120
Just in time.

11
00:01:24,200 --> 00:01:26,440
Didn't you want me to find someone
to practice on? I've found someone.

12
00:01:29,280 --> 00:01:30,520
It's too late to change your mind.

13
00:01:31,320 --> 00:01:32,880
You're in this with me now.

14
00:01:32,960 --> 00:01:34,080
Just teach me.

15
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:37,720
Understand?

16
00:01:41,920 --> 00:01:43,560
Our whole family has searched for a cure.

17
00:01:43,880 --> 00:01:45,360
Those great doctors and healers failed,

18
00:01:45,480 --> 00:01:48,360
but he can?
Do you take me for a three-year-old?

19
00:01:48,640 --> 00:01:50,840
I'd heard
your condition was beyond treatment.

20
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:52,720
When I took your pulse the other night,

21
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:54,160
I felt a faint sign of strength.

22
00:01:54,240 --> 00:01:55,760
There's still hope of recovery.

23
00:01:56,120 --> 00:01:58,440
You're nothing but
a dog kept by my uncle's family.

24
00:01:58,760 --> 00:02:00,120
We don't even feed you.

25
00:02:00,280 --> 00:02:02,040
How could I trust you to guard my door?

26
00:02:02,960 --> 00:02:04,200
We each get what we need.

27
00:02:04,400 --> 00:02:05,880
Lady Jin promised me something in return.

28
00:02:06,360 --> 00:02:07,560
What?

29
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:11,200
A letter recommending him
for the medical exam in the capital.

30
00:02:11,640 --> 00:02:12,880
Your letter alone is no use.

31
00:02:12,960 --> 00:02:14,640
It needs Grandmother's seal.

32
00:02:14,720 --> 00:02:17,720
I know. But if he cures Yan's legs,

33
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:18,920
would Grandmother refuse?

34
00:02:23,960 --> 00:02:25,160
You'd better not try anything.

35
00:02:25,240 --> 00:02:27,120
You talk too much.

36
00:02:29,480 --> 00:02:30,480
Hold still.

37
00:02:30,560 --> 00:02:31,560
Look.

38
00:02:31,640 --> 00:02:32,640
Like this.

39
00:02:32,720 --> 00:02:33,840
Just as I told you last time,
follow the meridians.

40
00:02:33,920 --> 00:02:35,240
Along the meridians.

41
00:02:38,640 --> 00:02:40,200
Why can't I feel that pulse now?

42
00:02:40,720 --> 00:02:42,000
What else did you do that day?

43
00:02:42,920 --> 00:02:45,960
That day, I was beaten, too.

44
00:02:46,120 --> 00:02:48,840
Anything else?
Was anything different from usual?

45
00:02:50,640 --> 00:02:56,760
No. You can go.

46
00:03:08,680 --> 00:03:09,920
I didn't use the medicine that day.

47
00:03:14,440 --> 00:03:16,720
Who gave you this medicine?
How long have you been using it?

48
00:03:17,400 --> 00:03:18,720
Someone from the second branch.

49
00:03:19,760 --> 00:03:21,160
Lady Qin found the prescription.

50
00:03:22,040 --> 00:03:23,440
Grandmother even praised her for it.

51
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:26,400
Could they be trying to poison you?

52
00:03:26,960 --> 00:03:29,880
Come on! Let's go to Grandmother
right now and report them!

53
00:03:29,960 --> 00:03:32,320
Wait. Think before you act.

54
00:03:33,120 --> 00:03:34,480
If there were something wrong with it,

55
00:03:35,160 --> 00:03:37,400
why didn't our doctors and healers notice?

56
00:03:37,480 --> 00:03:40,200
But… What if they were paid off?

57
00:03:40,280 --> 00:03:42,520
Or afraid of getting involved,
so they kept their mouths shut?

58
00:03:42,840 --> 00:03:43,960
Let's go. Let's go.

59
00:03:44,800 --> 00:03:46,320
Not everyone is a coward.

60
00:03:47,280 --> 00:03:48,320
However foolish they are,

61
00:03:49,240 --> 00:03:50,840
surely they wouldn't go that far.

62
00:03:53,880 --> 00:03:54,960
You should go.

63
00:04:00,960 --> 00:04:03,120
Listen to me. Listen to me.

64
00:04:04,120 --> 00:04:05,280
Once your legs are better,

65
00:04:05,480 --> 00:04:07,600
I'll show you off
at the shipping festival.

66
00:04:07,680 --> 00:04:08,840
Just think how grand we'd look!

67
00:04:09,560 --> 00:04:10,600
Don't forget,

68
00:04:11,640 --> 00:04:13,160
you haven't finished your lessons.

69
00:04:15,520 --> 00:04:18,000
How about this?
Stop using the medicine for a while,

70
00:04:18,160 --> 00:04:19,320
and I'll massage your legs again.

71
00:04:19,520 --> 00:04:20,880
What if there's a chance?

72
00:04:21,520 --> 00:04:22,520
Once your legs are better,

73
00:04:22,640 --> 00:04:24,400
we can expose them then.

74
00:04:26,880 --> 00:04:28,400
What chance could I possibly have?

75
00:04:29,720 --> 00:04:30,960
There is one.

76
00:04:42,920 --> 00:04:45,120
This is moxa.
The <i>Compendium of Materia Medica</i> says:

77
00:04:45,400 --> 00:04:47,160
"Mugwort is bitter and pungent,
warm when raw, hot when processed."

78
00:04:47,240 --> 00:04:48,960
"It is purely yang and nontoxic."

79
00:04:50,440 --> 00:04:52,480
If there's nothing wrong with it,
give it back to Yan.

80
00:04:52,640 --> 00:04:53,800
You keep making a fuss over nothing.

81
00:04:53,880 --> 00:04:54,880
I almost believed you!

82
00:04:56,080 --> 00:04:57,240
If the medicine's fine,

83
00:04:57,400 --> 00:04:59,280
why aren't Yan's legs
getting any better?

84
00:04:59,360 --> 00:05:01,080
He must stop using it, whatever it is.

85
00:05:01,160 --> 00:05:03,960
What's wrong with it?
Anyone can talk.

86
00:05:04,040 --> 00:05:05,840
If you're so capable, get him on his feet!

87
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:08,920
You're right, young master.

88
00:05:09,320 --> 00:05:10,600
If I were that capable,

89
00:05:11,200 --> 00:05:12,440
I wouldn't be living off someone else.

90
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:14,760
Unless we try, how will we know?

91
00:05:15,320 --> 00:05:17,520
Just as you fail time and again,
yet keep trying.

92
00:05:17,800 --> 00:05:19,560
If you can do it, why can't anyone else?

93
00:05:20,120 --> 00:05:21,680
Isn't that rather unfair?

94
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:37,320
Lady Jin, what is the meaning of this?

95
00:05:39,800 --> 00:05:42,280
Before,
I didn't apply myself to my lessons.

96
00:05:43,080 --> 00:05:45,280
My rashness got me confined by my lady,

97
00:05:45,760 --> 00:05:47,040
and by breaking the rules,

98
00:05:48,160 --> 00:05:49,640
I got my husband punished, too.

99
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:51,040
I feel ashamed.

100
00:05:51,320 --> 00:05:52,640
I want to make amends.

101
00:05:53,280 --> 00:05:55,040
I spent all night embroidering this.

102
00:05:55,120 --> 00:05:56,360
I know it isn't pretty,

103
00:05:56,560 --> 00:05:57,880
but I've done my best.

104
00:05:58,400 --> 00:05:59,760
Please teach me, Matron Fang.

105
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:06,360
Swallows are the hardest to embroider.

106
00:06:06,640 --> 00:06:07,960
Their colors are rich,

107
00:06:08,240 --> 00:06:10,160
but their movements are light.

108
00:06:10,720 --> 00:06:12,640
The stitches must be close, never stiff,

109
00:06:12,880 --> 00:06:14,000
loose, but never untidy.

110
00:06:15,160 --> 00:06:17,200
I'm not skilled enough.

111
00:06:17,720 --> 00:06:19,360
Find yourself a better teacher.

112
00:06:19,440 --> 00:06:22,280
Matron Fang, Madam promised me

113
00:06:22,680 --> 00:06:24,200
that once I'd completed your lessons,

114
00:06:24,320 --> 00:06:26,560
my husband and I could go
to the shipping festival.

115
00:06:27,320 --> 00:06:28,400
It's not just for myself.

116
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:29,960
I want to bring honor to the Xies.

117
00:06:30,400 --> 00:06:31,520
She said

118
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:33,120
your embroidery's poor,
and she won't teach you.

119
00:06:33,200 --> 00:06:34,760
What's the point of pestering her?

120
00:06:35,280 --> 00:06:37,280
Look, Matron Fang. I embroidered this.

121
00:06:38,600 --> 00:06:39,840
You're right, Miss Xi.

122
00:06:40,200 --> 00:06:42,000
I'm too impatient, unlike you.

123
00:06:42,400 --> 00:06:43,760
I still have much to learn.

124
00:06:43,920 --> 00:06:45,280
But things change so quickly.

125
00:06:45,360 --> 00:06:46,800
How can we know unless we try?

126
00:06:47,080 --> 00:06:48,160
Just like you,

127
00:06:48,280 --> 00:06:49,840
you fail time and again,
yet keep trying.

128
00:06:50,160 --> 00:06:51,600
If you can do it, why can't anyone else?

129
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:53,160
Isn't that rather unfair?

130
00:06:55,400 --> 00:06:56,800
Jin Baozhu! You--

131
00:06:57,760 --> 00:06:58,840
A lady keeps her composure.

132
00:06:59,280 --> 00:07:00,880
Please remember that, Miss Xi.

133
00:07:02,040 --> 00:07:03,120
Go back now.

134
00:07:05,320 --> 00:07:06,440
Yes.

135
00:07:11,920 --> 00:07:12,920
Please teach me.

136
00:07:13,400 --> 00:07:14,880
You're a hopeless block of wood,

137
00:07:15,400 --> 00:07:17,600
but at least you know to keep asking.

138
00:07:18,640 --> 00:07:19,680
Come in.

139
00:07:20,200 --> 00:07:23,000
Let's see if I can carve you into shape.

140
00:08:01,280 --> 00:08:02,360
Like this.

141
00:08:19,320 --> 00:08:21,040
It's not that cold. Leave it open.

142
00:08:25,920 --> 00:08:26,960
Once winter's over,

143
00:08:27,400 --> 00:08:28,680
spring won't be far behind.

144
00:08:43,040 --> 00:08:44,200
What are you up to now?

145
00:08:44,640 --> 00:08:46,120
Always running off somewhere.

146
00:08:47,040 --> 00:08:48,200
I'm learning my manners,

147
00:08:48,400 --> 00:08:49,640
so I can show off properly.

148
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:51,560
Lessons that keep you out past midnight?

149
00:09:09,560 --> 00:09:11,680
Jin Baozhu!
Who's this man you've brought home?

150
00:09:17,200 --> 00:09:20,000
Jin Baozhu!
Who's this man you've brought home?

151
00:09:26,720 --> 00:09:28,680
Where did this come from?

152
00:09:29,200 --> 00:09:30,520
The tree they cut down in the courtyard.

153
00:09:30,920 --> 00:09:31,920
What did you make it for?

154
00:09:34,160 --> 00:09:35,440
Because I wanted to.

155
00:09:35,960 --> 00:09:37,120
Go on. Go.

156
00:09:43,560 --> 00:09:44,640
You…

157
00:09:48,760 --> 00:09:50,120
I already told you

158
00:09:50,240 --> 00:09:51,360
not to waste your time.

159
00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:54,240
Why won't you listen?

160
00:09:54,680 --> 00:09:56,160
Besides, what sort of person

161
00:09:56,240 --> 00:09:57,400
keeps this thing in their room?

162
00:09:58,320 --> 00:09:59,880
Won't it give you nightmares?

163
00:10:00,440 --> 00:10:01,480
Throw it out.

164
00:10:01,560 --> 00:10:02,560
I'm not afraid.

165
00:10:03,160 --> 00:10:04,480
I'm afraid your legs won't get better.

166
00:10:10,400 --> 00:10:11,640
I will say it!

167
00:10:12,280 --> 00:10:14,000
A wound heals faster in the open.

168
00:10:14,120 --> 00:10:15,600
You can't cover it up forever

169
00:10:15,680 --> 00:10:16,800
and let it rot inside.

170
00:10:33,480 --> 00:10:34,600
That's not what I meant.

171
00:10:34,720 --> 00:10:35,880
I know.

172
00:10:37,080 --> 00:10:38,720
But there are things

173
00:10:39,840 --> 00:10:40,960
you don't know.

174
00:10:56,080 --> 00:10:57,200
Here.

175
00:11:16,320 --> 00:11:18,120
How could falling from a horse
leave you so badly hurt?

176
00:11:19,200 --> 00:11:20,360
Here, on my calf,

177
00:11:22,200 --> 00:11:24,320
iron shackles cut deep into the flesh.

178
00:11:25,240 --> 00:11:26,720
Once they were taken off,

179
00:11:27,040 --> 00:11:28,720
they left this deep groove.

180
00:11:33,560 --> 00:11:34,680
And here, my knee.

181
00:11:36,600 --> 00:11:39,080
They smashed the kneecap.

182
00:11:41,720 --> 00:11:42,760
It can never heal.

183
00:11:48,280 --> 00:11:49,440
On my thigh,

184
00:11:51,200 --> 00:11:53,080
a branding iron was pressed deep.

185
00:11:53,880 --> 00:11:55,440
Scabs crowded together,

186
00:11:55,800 --> 00:11:56,960
layer upon layer.

187
00:11:58,400 --> 00:11:59,960
You don't know.

188
00:12:01,320 --> 00:12:02,880
But I do.

189
00:12:04,760 --> 00:12:06,920
I know they're hideous enough
to turn your stomach.

190
00:12:07,800 --> 00:12:08,880
I know...

191
00:12:10,840 --> 00:12:12,440
you'll run when you see them.

192
00:12:17,520 --> 00:12:18,640
Frightened?

193
00:12:24,920 --> 00:12:26,080
Then leave.

194
00:12:50,600 --> 00:12:51,760
You don't know.

195
00:12:52,880 --> 00:12:54,280
You don't know that I'll stay,

196
00:12:55,080 --> 00:12:57,400
You don't know
that I'll hold your hand.

197
00:12:58,760 --> 00:13:00,320
And you don't know that one day,

198
00:13:00,840 --> 00:13:02,080
I'll heal your legs.

199
00:13:03,520 --> 00:13:04,800
But I do.

200
00:13:05,600 --> 00:13:06,840
Xie Yan,

201
00:13:07,640 --> 00:13:08,640
I've known you

202
00:13:09,480 --> 00:13:11,120
far longer than you realize.

203
00:13:13,160 --> 00:13:15,680
Even a great scholar

204
00:13:16,120 --> 00:13:17,560
can't know everything.

205
00:13:19,520 --> 00:13:20,640
Aren't you afraid?

206
00:13:21,760 --> 00:13:22,920
No.

207
00:13:23,720 --> 00:13:24,760
But I am.

208
00:13:28,720 --> 00:13:29,880
Things have changed.

209
00:13:31,360 --> 00:13:32,840
I'm no longer

210
00:13:34,560 --> 00:13:36,600
the Xie Yan who rode through the streets.

211
00:13:38,720 --> 00:13:39,800
Things have changed.

212
00:13:40,560 --> 00:13:42,760
My embroidered swallows
are quite good now.

213
00:13:52,840 --> 00:13:54,440
Yet you still don't believe in me.

214
00:14:16,480 --> 00:14:17,880
I gave you a chance.

215
00:14:19,720 --> 00:14:21,760
You walked into my trap yourself.

216
00:14:34,520 --> 00:14:36,160
You called us here to see this?

217
00:14:37,040 --> 00:14:38,960
You're so fond of Yan.
You can have it.

218
00:14:39,040 --> 00:14:40,360
Cuddle it in bed at night.

219
00:14:40,440 --> 00:14:42,400
You're mad! I don't want it!

220
00:14:42,760 --> 00:14:44,920
Besides,
didn't you need someone to practice on?

221
00:14:45,880 --> 00:14:47,640
I've found someone better suited.

222
00:14:53,720 --> 00:14:55,440
-My lord.
-Yan.

223
00:14:56,320 --> 00:14:57,920
I know about the letter.

224
00:14:58,480 --> 00:14:59,640
Thank you for doing this.

225
00:14:59,960 --> 00:15:01,080
Thank you.

226
00:15:12,160 --> 00:15:13,760
Your pulse is sluggish and hard as stone.

227
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:16,240
Qi and blood can't reach your legs.

228
00:15:17,520 --> 00:15:18,520
How strange.

229
00:15:20,120 --> 00:15:21,720
All those doctors and healers

230
00:15:22,680 --> 00:15:24,000
said just the same.

231
00:15:40,040 --> 00:15:41,080
Benzoin.

232
00:15:42,640 --> 00:15:44,440
That's the root of your trouble.

233
00:15:45,720 --> 00:15:47,000
What nonsense are you talking?

234
00:15:47,240 --> 00:15:48,920
My mother prepared that
benzoin especially for him.

235
00:15:50,360 --> 00:15:51,960
Benzoin revives the senses.

236
00:15:52,640 --> 00:15:56,040
Moxa warms and opens the meridians,
dispels cold, and eases pain.

237
00:15:56,360 --> 00:15:58,320
Used separately, both are good medicines.

238
00:15:59,400 --> 00:16:01,520
But together,
it's a different matter entirely.

239
00:16:01,800 --> 00:16:03,200
Benzoin spreads rapidly through the body.

240
00:16:03,280 --> 00:16:04,520
Moxa is warming and potent.

241
00:16:04,760 --> 00:16:07,040
The two together
are like pouring oil on a fire.

242
00:16:07,400 --> 00:16:09,480
At first, inhaling it
brings relief throughout the body.

243
00:16:09,560 --> 00:16:10,800
Over time, they deplete
the blood and body fluids,

244
00:16:10,880 --> 00:16:11,880
causing chronic illness.

245
00:16:12,600 --> 00:16:14,840
How long have you used it?

246
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:16,120
Have you used it continuously?

247
00:16:17,400 --> 00:16:18,560
Ever since I fell ill.

248
00:16:18,760 --> 00:16:19,800
Once in the morning, once at night,

249
00:16:20,760 --> 00:16:22,160
and again in damp or rainy weather.

250
00:16:22,520 --> 00:16:24,320
Except for the night you took my pulse,

251
00:16:24,680 --> 00:16:26,120
I've never missed a dose.

252
00:16:26,320 --> 00:16:29,040
That explains it.
It may calm you and ease the pain,

253
00:16:29,120 --> 00:16:30,160
but it's addictive.

254
00:16:30,840 --> 00:16:32,640
The meridians in your legs
are severely blocked.

255
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:35,480
Ordinary massage
probably won't help.

256
00:16:35,920 --> 00:16:37,320
First, moxibustion to open the meridians,

257
00:16:37,560 --> 00:16:38,760
together with acupressure.

258
00:16:39,160 --> 00:16:40,320
Then we can make gradual progress.

259
00:16:41,080 --> 00:16:44,520
But there's one difficult thing
to do first.

260
00:16:48,080 --> 00:16:49,280
If you're giving up the medicine,

261
00:16:50,160 --> 00:16:51,440
all of this has to go.

262
00:16:59,600 --> 00:17:00,680
Why are you looking at me?

263
00:17:00,920 --> 00:17:03,160
If you weren't looking at me,
how would you know?

264
00:17:12,680 --> 00:17:13,800
Later tonight…

265
00:17:17,200 --> 00:17:18,280
Once the lights are out…

266
00:17:23,120 --> 00:17:24,320
It's all right.

267
00:18:36,840 --> 00:18:37,880
Ask Jianwei to fetch some.

268
00:18:38,560 --> 00:18:39,600
Just a little will do.

269
00:18:39,960 --> 00:18:41,640
Hold on. Just a little longer.

270
00:18:49,080 --> 00:18:51,320
I want some soup.

271
00:18:52,520 --> 00:18:55,280
Jianwei, ask the kitchen
to make some soup.

272
00:18:55,360 --> 00:18:56,920
Yingtao, get a fresh basin of water.

273
00:18:57,160 --> 00:18:58,160
-Yes.
-This month's private allowance

274
00:18:58,240 --> 00:18:59,240
has all gone on medicine.

275
00:18:59,320 --> 00:19:00,480
It's not mealtime.

276
00:19:00,560 --> 00:19:01,640
They won't give us anything.

277
00:19:04,760 --> 00:19:05,880
I'll go and ask.

278
00:19:06,920 --> 00:19:07,920
Watch him.

279
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:09,520
Shut the doors and windows
before it rains.

280
00:19:09,600 --> 00:19:10,760
Yes.

281
00:19:12,120 --> 00:19:13,400
My lord.

282
00:19:13,680 --> 00:19:14,920
My lord, hold on!

283
00:19:16,400 --> 00:19:17,920
My lord! My lord.

284
00:19:30,760 --> 00:19:31,760
My lady. My lady, I…

285
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:33,640
-Why have you come out?
-My lord's asleep.

286
00:19:33,840 --> 00:19:35,120
Let me carry that, my lady.

287
00:19:37,880 --> 00:19:39,480
My lady! My lady!

288
00:19:40,360 --> 00:19:41,520
Xie Yan!

289
00:19:51,240 --> 00:19:53,000
Do you know,
just to get what you asked for,

290
00:19:53,080 --> 00:19:54,280
how long I had to beg?

291
00:19:54,920 --> 00:19:56,240
You only wanted me out of the way

292
00:19:56,320 --> 00:19:58,200
so you could do this!
You…

293
00:20:06,080 --> 00:20:07,200
You fool!

294
00:20:08,040 --> 00:20:09,600
All you say is to bear it.

295
00:20:10,760 --> 00:20:12,120
All of you tell me to bear it!

296
00:20:12,440 --> 00:20:13,600
It's not your face being slapped,

297
00:20:13,680 --> 00:20:14,840
so you don't feel the pain!

298
00:20:23,600 --> 00:20:24,720
Don't blame him, my lady.

299
00:20:24,960 --> 00:20:27,200
It was me. He couldn't bear it anymore,

300
00:20:27,280 --> 00:20:28,560
so I gave him an empty pipe.

301
00:20:29,560 --> 00:20:31,400
He didn't want you to see him like this.

302
00:20:32,120 --> 00:20:33,480
That's why he sent you away.

303
00:20:37,080 --> 00:20:39,840
I… I hate you, Jin Baozhu!

304
00:20:43,720 --> 00:20:44,880
Go away!

305
00:21:18,880 --> 00:21:19,920
I'm sorry.

306
00:21:22,480 --> 00:21:23,520
I'm sorry.

307
00:21:23,800 --> 00:21:25,160
Hate me, then.

308
00:21:25,960 --> 00:21:27,360
I'm not leaving.

309
00:21:28,080 --> 00:21:29,840
Even if you hate me, I'm staying.

310
00:21:30,200 --> 00:21:31,400
I want you to stand,

311
00:21:31,840 --> 00:21:33,160
taller than anyone.

312
00:22:08,360 --> 00:22:10,320
Lady Jin really cares about your master.

313
00:22:10,960 --> 00:22:12,920
She came through the rain to fetch me.

314
00:22:14,920 --> 00:22:17,080
I don't think I'm needed now.

315
00:22:18,200 --> 00:22:20,680
May I ask when my lord will recover?

316
00:22:22,800 --> 00:22:24,560
His legs can already move.

317
00:22:25,080 --> 00:22:26,640
But he's under too much mental strain.

318
00:22:27,440 --> 00:22:28,800
He needs to keep practicing.

319
00:22:41,960 --> 00:22:43,240
I can't even stand steadily.

320
00:22:43,720 --> 00:22:44,960
How am I supposed to practice?

321
00:22:45,520 --> 00:22:46,920
Close your eyes first.

322
00:23:07,240 --> 00:23:08,600
Practice in your mind.

323
00:23:08,880 --> 00:23:10,120
In my mind?

324
00:23:11,280 --> 00:23:13,520
Imagine this. Every day,

325
00:23:13,680 --> 00:23:15,760
you work hard butchering pigs
and selling meat.

326
00:23:16,040 --> 00:23:19,560
Then, suddenly,
a thug snatches your purse.

327
00:23:20,200 --> 00:23:21,520
You're furious,

328
00:23:21,600 --> 00:23:22,880
but you're so tired.

329
00:23:22,960 --> 00:23:24,240
Still, you have to chase him.

330
00:23:24,320 --> 00:23:27,040
So you lift your left foot,

331
00:23:27,480 --> 00:23:28,840
then your right.

332
00:23:29,240 --> 00:23:30,480
Left foot, right foot.

333
00:23:31,080 --> 00:23:32,920
Left foot, right foot.

334
00:23:33,480 --> 00:23:35,200
Left, right.

335
00:23:35,760 --> 00:23:39,280
Left, right. Left, right. Left, right.

336
00:23:39,360 --> 00:23:41,320
Walk faster and faster.
Faster and faster.

337
00:23:41,400 --> 00:23:42,560
Run faster and faster.
Faster and faster.

338
00:23:43,080 --> 00:23:45,040
At last, you catch up with him.

339
00:23:45,120 --> 00:23:46,600
He swings a punch at you,

340
00:23:46,680 --> 00:23:49,120
so you dodge quickly, left and right,

341
00:23:49,440 --> 00:23:51,920
with quick little steps,
until you've dodged the blow.

342
00:23:52,320 --> 00:23:54,000
You plant your feet, lift your leg,

343
00:23:54,200 --> 00:23:56,120
and launch a flying kick.
You kick him away.

344
00:23:56,840 --> 00:23:57,880
Congratulations!

345
00:23:58,840 --> 00:24:00,280
You've got your purse back.

346
00:24:07,000 --> 00:24:08,960
Ridiculous. Are we playing house?

347
00:24:09,040 --> 00:24:10,160
What do you know?

348
00:24:10,640 --> 00:24:11,920
There's a method to this.

349
00:24:12,160 --> 00:24:13,480
Whether I strike the front or back,

350
00:24:13,560 --> 00:24:15,360
hard, slowly, or not at all,

351
00:24:15,560 --> 00:24:16,920
each tells you to lift your leg,

352
00:24:17,000 --> 00:24:18,200
move, or hold still.

353
00:24:18,280 --> 00:24:20,200
Every day, listen to the drumbeats

354
00:24:20,360 --> 00:24:21,360
and practice in your mind.

355
00:24:21,680 --> 00:24:22,800
Think it through, day and night.

356
00:24:22,880 --> 00:24:24,120
Once your mind finds its way,

357
00:24:24,200 --> 00:24:26,520
your legs will follow. Well?

358
00:24:28,280 --> 00:24:29,640
Let's try again.

359
00:24:30,960 --> 00:24:32,960
Have you got another story?

360
00:24:33,040 --> 00:24:35,120
Of course. Besides chasing thugs,

361
00:24:35,200 --> 00:24:36,800
there's chasing ruffians,

362
00:24:37,000 --> 00:24:39,520
carts, or wild dogs.
What would you like to chase?

363
00:24:53,040 --> 00:24:54,120
Serve the tea.

364
00:25:28,360 --> 00:25:32,320
Smooth, with a lingering sweetness.

365
00:25:33,680 --> 00:25:37,160
Very good.
You're really getting the hang of it.

366
00:25:38,240 --> 00:25:40,040
What brings you here?

367
00:25:40,880 --> 00:25:43,840
You said that once I'd learned my manners,

368
00:25:43,920 --> 00:25:45,440
I could go to the shipping festival.

369
00:25:46,240 --> 00:25:48,560
Does that still stand?

370
00:25:57,760 --> 00:25:58,960
Grain Transport Wharf
The Bai family

371
00:26:02,000 --> 00:26:03,360
So that's what you're after?

372
00:26:03,440 --> 00:26:04,440
Yes.

373
00:26:04,520 --> 00:26:06,320
Move aside! Move aside!

374
00:26:07,000 --> 00:26:08,320
-Who's that?
-My master has a contest to get to!

375
00:26:08,480 --> 00:26:10,040
Move! Out of the way!

376
00:26:10,120 --> 00:26:11,120
Really?

377
00:26:11,320 --> 00:26:12,400
Move!

378
00:26:13,040 --> 00:26:14,320
This way, my lord.

379
00:26:19,520 --> 00:26:20,560
It's all right.

380
00:26:20,640 --> 00:26:22,120
Who's that?
Who tripped me?

381
00:26:25,280 --> 00:26:26,280
This…

382
00:26:26,360 --> 00:26:30,440
Chengjiang, how have you been?

383
00:26:36,160 --> 00:26:37,840
Master Bai. Master Huang.

384
00:26:38,240 --> 00:26:39,280
It's been a while.

385
00:26:50,200 --> 00:26:53,760
Junmei, that trip just now
seemed rather suspicious.

386
00:26:54,320 --> 00:26:55,320
Can you prove it?

387
00:26:57,440 --> 00:26:58,840
Unless you're sure you can win,

388
00:26:59,040 --> 00:27:00,720
you shouldn't pick a fight.

389
00:27:01,080 --> 00:27:03,520
Besides, if a dog bites you,

390
00:27:04,080 --> 00:27:05,520
do you bite it back?

391
00:27:05,600 --> 00:27:06,720
Huang Yulan
The Huang family's eldest legitimate son

392
00:27:11,160 --> 00:27:12,720
Why haven't the ladies of your house

393
00:27:12,800 --> 00:27:14,160
joined us today?

394
00:27:15,840 --> 00:27:16,960
Please, have some.

395
00:27:17,560 --> 00:27:19,360
The shops are packed at festival time.

396
00:27:19,480 --> 00:27:21,280
They've all gone to help out there,

397
00:27:21,360 --> 00:27:22,520
and can't get away.

398
00:27:27,240 --> 00:27:29,760
Nangong's Five Talents

399
00:27:30,040 --> 00:27:31,680
It's a promise. Don't forget!

400
00:27:32,040 --> 00:27:33,760
Mother.

401
00:27:34,000 --> 00:27:36,600
Let the ceremony begin!

402
00:27:36,720 --> 00:27:38,560
Grain Transport Wharf

403
00:27:59,080 --> 00:28:02,000
Today, at the shipping festival,

404
00:28:02,480 --> 00:28:05,960
the whole city has gathered.

405
00:28:06,040 --> 00:28:09,120
I join the people of this prefecture

406
00:28:09,200 --> 00:28:11,080
in celebrating together.

407
00:28:11,400 --> 00:28:13,960
There will be three contests.

408
00:28:14,400 --> 00:28:17,400
Each of Yangzhou's four great families
in grain transport

409
00:28:17,480 --> 00:28:21,240
shall send four representatives
to compete.

410
00:28:21,520 --> 00:28:24,080
The lowest-scoring family
is eliminated each round.

411
00:28:24,200 --> 00:28:25,840
The last family standing

412
00:28:25,920 --> 00:28:28,360
will be this year's champion.

413
00:28:28,680 --> 00:28:30,160
This year, in the Huaiyang Circuit,

414
00:28:30,240 --> 00:28:31,760
the largest shipping contract

415
00:28:31,840 --> 00:28:35,000
will go entirely to the winning family.

416
00:28:38,000 --> 00:28:41,280
Let the contest begin!

417
00:28:41,360 --> 00:28:42,800
Grain Transport Wharf

418
00:28:43,600 --> 00:28:45,080
Those two, one's a Huang, one's a Bai.

419
00:28:45,160 --> 00:28:46,360
How are they on the same team?

420
00:28:47,640 --> 00:28:49,240
They're cousins, after a fashion.

421
00:28:50,840 --> 00:28:52,600
One sailor is at the mainmast,

422
00:28:52,680 --> 00:28:53,920
flying a blue flag.

423
00:28:54,200 --> 00:28:57,400
Another hangs a white flag
at an angle on the secondary mast.

424
00:28:57,680 --> 00:28:59,160
One sailor stands at the bow,

425
00:28:59,240 --> 00:29:01,840
fingers together, hand at chest height,

426
00:29:01,920 --> 00:29:03,160
palm facing down,

427
00:29:03,240 --> 00:29:04,720
and presses down three times.

428
00:29:05,080 --> 00:29:07,160
What does it mean?

429
00:29:10,680 --> 00:29:13,080
That's easy.
Our convoy proceeds as normal.

430
00:29:13,160 --> 00:29:14,720
The first three ships slow down in stages.

431
00:29:14,800 --> 00:29:16,760
Close up the rear. No overtaking.

432
00:29:19,760 --> 00:29:21,040
The Xie family
The Bai family

433
00:29:21,160 --> 00:29:22,520
A sailor at the mainmast

434
00:29:22,600 --> 00:29:24,800
raises a red flag bearing a black blade.

435
00:29:25,240 --> 00:29:27,840
Another waves a yellow flag at the bow

436
00:29:27,920 --> 00:29:29,320
in wide sweeps.

437
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:31,400
The orders conflict.

438
00:29:31,480 --> 00:29:33,520
Which takes priority?

439
00:29:33,640 --> 00:29:35,880
Enemy ahead! All hands fight!

440
00:29:36,160 --> 00:29:37,320
First, form up to repel the pirates,

441
00:29:37,480 --> 00:29:38,720
then save the ship.

442
00:29:39,440 --> 00:29:41,000
A sailor at the bow

443
00:29:41,080 --> 00:29:43,160
strikes a small gong hard three times.

444
00:29:43,240 --> 00:29:45,920
Close ranks? Pass through a lock?

445
00:29:46,120 --> 00:29:47,760
Or give way?

446
00:29:50,120 --> 00:29:52,000
Fog ahead. Close ranks.
Stay within earshot of nearby ships.

447
00:29:52,200 --> 00:29:53,240
Take great care.

448
00:29:53,320 --> 00:29:55,280
Grain Transport Wharf

449
00:29:55,520 --> 00:29:56,960
Xie family, 12 points.

450
00:29:57,040 --> 00:29:58,440
Bai family, 10 points.

451
00:29:58,520 --> 00:29:59,760
Su family, seven points.

452
00:29:59,840 --> 00:30:01,160
Yang family, six points.

453
00:30:01,280 --> 00:30:02,640
The Yang family is eliminated.

454
00:30:02,720 --> 00:30:04,920
Good! Good! Good!

455
00:30:05,280 --> 00:30:06,320
Good!

456
00:30:06,960 --> 00:30:08,040
Good!

457
00:30:08,200 --> 00:30:11,240
Load the hold. Stack and tie the grain.

458
00:30:11,320 --> 00:30:12,760
This round is Loading the Hold.

459
00:30:13,520 --> 00:30:16,720
Your allotted area is your grain ship.

460
00:30:16,800 --> 00:30:18,320
Before this incense stick burns out,

461
00:30:18,520 --> 00:30:19,680
load your grain.

462
00:30:20,160 --> 00:30:21,760
When the incense runs out,

463
00:30:22,040 --> 00:30:25,600
the ship with the least grain is out.

464
00:30:31,120 --> 00:30:32,240
Out of my way!

465
00:30:45,280 --> 00:30:46,640
Have you heard the saying,

466
00:30:46,800 --> 00:30:49,160
"When two fight,
a third takes the prize"?

467
00:30:49,240 --> 00:30:50,240
Then have you heard how

468
00:30:50,320 --> 00:30:52,560
Tian Ji won a horse race
by giving up a little to win big?

469
00:30:55,520 --> 00:30:56,760
What race? On a farm?

470
00:30:57,520 --> 00:30:58,920
Tian Ji's horse race.

471
00:30:59,480 --> 00:31:01,480
Send your worst horse against their best,

472
00:31:01,560 --> 00:31:03,560
your best against their middle horse,

473
00:31:03,640 --> 00:31:05,520
and your middle horse against their worst.

474
00:31:05,840 --> 00:31:07,480
Let weaker horses face stronger ones,
and stronger horses beat weaker ones.

475
00:31:07,560 --> 00:31:09,160
Give up a battle to win the war,

476
00:31:09,240 --> 00:31:10,480
and turn defeat into victory.

477
00:31:10,960 --> 00:31:12,240
Heng is very capable,

478
00:31:12,480 --> 00:31:15,320
but his old illness has flared up.

479
00:31:15,520 --> 00:31:16,560
I'm all right.

480
00:31:19,960 --> 00:31:21,880
Madam, let me take Heng's place.

481
00:31:21,960 --> 00:31:23,600
No. My son can win this.

482
00:31:23,840 --> 00:31:25,200
What do we need you for?

483
00:31:25,640 --> 00:31:27,680
Heng can't hold on much longer.

484
00:31:30,520 --> 00:31:32,280
-Perhaps…
-Mother! Mother!

485
00:31:32,360 --> 00:31:33,840
Think carefully about this.

486
00:31:33,920 --> 00:31:36,360
I believe my son can win, so he will!

487
00:31:36,640 --> 00:31:38,720
All the families are here today.

488
00:31:39,160 --> 00:31:40,720
If we replace him halfway through,

489
00:31:40,800 --> 00:31:43,200
then… what would they think of Heng?

490
00:31:43,280 --> 00:31:44,320
Don't you agree, Mother?

491
00:31:44,400 --> 00:31:46,520
The Bais are playing such dirty tricks.

492
00:31:46,600 --> 00:31:47,760
What have we got to be afraid of?

493
00:31:48,520 --> 00:31:50,760
Madam, please let me go!

494
00:31:50,840 --> 00:31:52,000
I've learned my manners.

495
00:31:52,080 --> 00:31:53,600
I won't disgrace the family.

496
00:31:54,640 --> 00:31:55,960
I promise.

497
00:31:55,960 --> 00:31:56,960

